A||N||5||fieroshop||Has this ever happen to you?||||10||
Z||000000||fieroshop||04-29-2000||10:48 PM||||Well here I am sitting at my desk talking with some new customers when I decide to call about a part that had not arrived as yet. I was told that the last truck had left and that I would need to send somebody to pick up the part. Since I was busy with customers I asked my wife to go to the parts store and pickup the part that was needed to finish another job as I was busy with customers and I had another customer waiting for an ignition module for his car.<BR>So off to the parts store she went and she took our two small dogs in her 86 GT to pick it up. <BR>A short time later I get a call and was told that it was the CHP and that my wife had broken down on the freeway and needed a tow. <BR>As the customer who was waiting for his part was there and he is also a friend I asked him if he would take my 88 GT and pick her up on the freeway and that when I unloaded the trailer which had an 86 GT that I had towed yesterday for an engine swap for a 3.4 I would go and pick up the Fiero.<BR>Well my freind and my wife get back and I get done with my other customers I get in the truck and go pickup the GT. When I get there I ask my wife to start the motor as the problem as I was told was the transmission failed. (Automatic)She starts the GT and I check the oil and find it full and clean so I tell her to put it in gear and the GT drives just fine. Well it seems that one of the dogs hit the shift lever causing it to go in neutral and so she pulled  of the road and a CHP officer pulled in behind her before she did anything else and so I was called. Results I did not have to replace a transmission saving a ton of work.I told her next time to just put the car in gear and keep going.||||reg||10
